## stagegate — how agents work in {{ project.name }}

This section is managed by stagegate-agents (`stagegate.toml`). Edit the
config and re-run the installer rather than editing between the markers.

### Delivery chain
`/feature-factory <idea>`: codebase-researcher → story-writer → **⛔ human approves story**
→ spec-writer → **⛔ human approves brief** → test-strategist → builders + test-verifier
→ implementation-validator (loop until 0 Critical) → **⛔ human approves implementation**
→ pr-reviewer → pull request → CI → merge gate.
{{#if infra.enabled}}`/infra-factory <change>` runs the same gates for {{ infra.iac_dir }}/, {{ infra.k8s_dir }}/ and .github/workflows/.
{{/if}}
Never skip a ⛔ gate. "Approved" must come from the human in this conversation.

### Stack
- Language: {{ stack.language }} (guidance: `stacks/{{ stack.profile }}.md`, installed as `.claude/stagegate/stack.md`)
- Code: `{{ stack.backend_dir }}`{{#if stack.frontend_dir}} · frontend: `{{ stack.frontend_dir }}`{{/if}} · tests: `{{ stack.tests_dir }}`
- Run tests: `{{#if stack.run_prefix}}{{ stack.run_prefix }} {{/if}}{{ stack.test_command }}`
- Lint: `{{#if stack.run_prefix}}{{ stack.run_prefix }} {{/if}}{{ stack.lint_command }}`

### Git
- Work on a branch named `{{ git.branch_prefix }}<slug>`; never commit to `{{ project.default_branch }}`.
- Commit style: {{ git.commit_style }}. Open a PR; never merge your own PR.
- A PR merges only when every CI check is green{{#if review.require_green_ci}} (enforced by the merge gate hook){{/if}}.

### Guardrails (enforced by hooks, not by this text)
- **Commit guard** blocks commits of secrets and state files{{#if guards.block_latest_tag}}, `:latest` image tags{{/if}}{{#if guards.forbidden_patterns}}, configured forbidden patterns{{/if}}.
- **Merge gate** blocks `gh pr merge` while any check is red, pending or missing.
- **Load-test guard** blocks load tools aimed at anything but local hosts.
{{#if sandbox.enabled}}- **Sandbox**: Bash runs in Claude Code's sandbox. Credential stores are unreadable and
  network access is limited to the allowed domains. Don't try to work around it: ask the human.
{{else}}- **Sandbox is OFF** (`sandbox.enabled = false`). Agents run with the developer's full permissions.
{{/if}}
If a guard blocks you, fix the cause. Never disable, bypass or edit a guard to get past it.

### Tests
- Every change ships with tests: success path, failure/auth path, not-found/edge path.
- Tests never call real external services (LLM APIs, GitHub, cloud): mock the clients.
- Load tests run against a local stack only, and only when the human asks.
